# ANALOGY:
Control File = Database Map
Data File    = Actual Data
Redo Log     = Changes
Archive Log  = Old Redo History
SPFILE       = Startup Settings
Alert Log    = Oracle Diary
Password File= SYSDBA Authentication
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE:
====
1. Oracle does not enforce fixed paths for these files.
2. Their locations depend on how the DBA installed Oracle and configured the database.
3. However, there are common default locations and every DBA should know what each file does.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FILES:
======
1. Data files:  Store actual table data, indexes, undo data, etc.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Typical Path: "/oracle/oradata/ORCL/"

Eg:
/oracle/oradata/ORCL/system01.dbf
/oracle/oradata/ORCL/users01.dbf

Check Location:
SELECT file_name
FROM dba_data_files;

Eg files:
users01.dbf
system01.dbf
sysaux01.dbf
undotbs01.dbf

2.Redo Log Files: Store every change made to the database.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Typical Path: "/oracle/oradata/ORCL/"

Eg:
/oracle/oradata/ORCL/redo01.log

Check Location:
SELECT member
FROM v$logfile;

Used for:
Crash recovery
Media recovery
Data protection

3. Control File: The brain/map of the database.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Typical Paths:
/oracle/oradata/ORCL/control01.ctl
/oracle/fast_recovery_area/ORCL/control02.ctl

Eg:
control01.ctl
control02.ctl
control03.ctl

Check Location:
SELECT name
FROM v$controlfile;

Contains:
Database name
Datafile locations
Redo log locations
Checkpoint information
SCN information
